  "description": "WILDOL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H63 Eu4 F27 O33,C4 H8 O2. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.661-4.536 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.56-141.53°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu4(η3-ETA)3(η2-ETA)6(μ3-OH)3(H2O)3]·(CH3CO2CH2CH3). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
